# Line endings that matter to the runtime, not to the editor.
#
# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers (scripts/dbt-entrypoint.sh
# is), and a CRLF checkout breaks them — including the heredoc terminator.
# Dockerfiles are worse: CRLF silently breaks a `RUN ... \` line continuation.
# Authoring happens on Windows, so pin these to LF in the repository.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
